					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 2: REACTION DIFFUSION\n\nReaction Diffusion is a mathematical model to generate patterns.\nWe can recreate the look of this model by using a feedback loop that blurs the image and sharpens it afterwards.\n\nIn this image we use Fractal Noise as a starting point.\nWe create a reset button by using two Snapshot nodes.\nFirst we fire off a 0 and 0.001 seconds later we fire off a 1 to reset all the layers.\n\nA Transform node is added to introduce some movement into the pattern."
					}
